# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the pgt::mpsc queue tests.
#
#   TSAN_OPTIONS="suppressions=cpp/test/tsan.supp" ./mpsc_test
#
# WHAT IS SUPPRESSED, AND WHY IT IS A DECISION RATHER THAN AN INCONVENIENCE.
#
# The suppressed reports are all one class: a stale walker's atomic probe of a
# descriptor slot -- the walk's acquire load, or a failed claim CAS (which TSan
# counts as a write access) -- landing on bytes that concurrently serve as
# another record's PAYLOAD, written and read with plain memcpy. This is
# inherent to in-band descriptors in a variable-length ring: a walker starting
# from a stale hint may compute a position that is currently interior to a live
# record, probe it, and discard the result. The protocol is safe by content,
# not by quiescence: a claim succeeds only against the exact freeWord(p) match
# (Lemma 1 in the algorithm spec), so a probe of garbage can never produce a
# valid claim, and the probed VALUE is never trusted -- only re-derived after
# an acquire re-read.
#
# Formally, plain-write + concurrent atomic-read of the same location is still
# a C++ data race, so TSan is right to report it and this file is the recorded
# decision to accept it (team-lead ruling, 2026-07-25).
#
# THE CHEAP FIX, RECORDED SO NOBODY REDISCOVERS IT: descriptors only ever sit
# at 64-byte (kGrain) boundaries, so only payload words at those offsets can be
# racily probed. Writing just those words with relaxed atomic stores -- one
# atomic store per 64 bytes of payload, the rest a plain memcpy -- would close
# the formal race. Judged not worth the hot-path cost today; revisit if a
# compiler or a non-TSO target ever gives a reason.
#
# SCOPE. Three rules because symbolization is not uniform across the shapes
# this class produces (verified empirically -- each rule has shapes only it
# matches, and together they take the suite to zero reports):
#   - race:pgt::mpsc::Ring       payload memcpy frames inside Ring::write /
#                                probes where the instantiation demangles with
#                                its qualified name ([[gnu::always_inline]]
#                                folds reserve into write, so the frame says
#                                write, not reserve).
#   - race:reserveSlow           instantiations over internal-linkage policies
#                                (anonymous-namespace test policies) symbolize
#                                as the BARE function name with no class.
#   - race:*/pgt/mpsc/queue.hh   frames where the file survived but the
#                                function name did not.
#
# WHAT THIS SHADOWS: a race whose stack passes through Ring code for any other
# reason -- notably a genuine payload-vs-payload overlap between two writers --
# is also suppressed. That class is independently caught by the differential
# and stress tests' CONTENT validation (overlapping payloads cannot both
# survive a byte-exact compare), which is why the shadow is acceptable. If the
# library ever grows a TSan-aware inlining knob and stable symbolization,
# tighten back to reserve/reserveSlow function rules only.
race:pgt::mpsc::Ring
race:reserveSlow
race:*/pgt/mpsc/queue.hh
